From: Johan Hovold <johan+linaro@kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: qca: fix device-address endianness

Backport the btqca helper fix from Linux commit
77f45cca8bc55d00520a192f5a7715133591c83e:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/77f45cca8bc55d00520a192f5a7715133591c83e

The QCA6390 firmware on this Neo3 likewise expects big-endian bytes for
EDL_WRITE_BD_ADDR_OPCODE. The unchanged btmgmt command currently results in
the reversed unit address. Convert the kernel's little-endian bdaddr_t at
the vendor-command boundary. The separate ROME callback stays unchanged.

Apply after experimental/0054-qca6390-tty.patch. Only the helper change is
needed for this explicit TTY/mgmt path; the upstream WCN3991 device-tree
compatibility changes are outside its scope.

Signed-off-by: Johan Hovold <johan+linaro@kernel.org>
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btqca.c
@@ -529,10 +529,14 @@
 int qca_set_bdaddr(struct hci_dev *hdev, const bdaddr_t *bdaddr)
 {
+	bdaddr_t bdaddr_swapped;
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 	int err;
 
-	skb = __hci_cmd_sync_ev(hdev, EDL_WRITE_BD_ADDR_OPCODE, 6, bdaddr,
-				HCI_EV_VENDOR, HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
+	baswap(&bdaddr_swapped, bdaddr);
+
+	skb = __hci_cmd_sync_ev(hdev, EDL_WRITE_BD_ADDR_OPCODE, 6,
+				&bdaddr_swapped, HCI_EV_VENDOR,
+				HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
 	if (IS_ERR(skb)) {
 		err = PTR_ERR(skb);
 		bt_dev_err(hdev, "QCA Change address cmd failed (%d)", err);
